/// Capabilities the TEE host provides to the policy live in the RESERVED
/// `enclavid:host` package, and in any `enclavid:host-*` one: a composed plugin
/// may `import` an interface there (reading the same host surface the policy
/// does), but it must never SATISFY one. Runtime fusion refuses to wire a plugin
/// export into a host-reserved import and rejects outright any plugin that
/// exports one — host interfaces are served exclusively by the TEE `Linker`.
/// New host capabilities land as new interfaces in these packages, so the trust
/// boundary stays a single prefix check rather than a denylist that must be kept
/// in sync.
///
/// `enclavid:host-icons` holds the icons the applicant frontend draws, in a
/// package of its own so that a new icon moves that package's version alone.
/// `enclavid:host-capture` and `enclavid:host-disclosure` hold the shapes the
/// host renders a capture and a consent screen from, each in a package of its
/// own so that each moves its own version.
///
/// What a component declares itself, because the types are its own, it
/// declares in its slot, a package of the `enclavid-ext` namespace the host
/// serves as well. Every component's texts: `enclavid-ext:<slot>/i18n`, whose
/// `key` enum has a case for each text and whose `localized` mints the text of
/// a case, served from the catalog that names the slot. A plugin's slot is named
/// for its package; the policy's is `enclavid-ext:policy`, which holds as well
/// `props`, whose `get` returns the props the consumer gave the session
/// in whatever record the policy declares for them, and `disclosure-fields`,
/// whose `key` lists the fields its disclosures may name. A component may import
/// another's texts by its slot.
///
/// A component's models: `enclavid-ext:<slot>/models`, a function for each ONNX
/// model its artifact carries beside its component — a layer `<function>.onnx`,
/// the graph, and where its weights are large `<function>.onnx.data`, the data
/// file the graph points into — returning a resource the slot declares, whose
/// one method `run` borrows a tensor of `enclavid:host/tensors` for each input
/// of the graph and returns one for each output: as itself, or a tuple or a
/// record of them for more than one. The host serves the resource: the model
/// runs in a process of its own beside the round, started the first time a
/// round calls the function. Only the one artifact that imports a slot's models
/// is served them, and only its own files.
package enclavid:host@0.1.0;

/// The handles the host mints for what a prompt is made of: RESOURCES a
/// component cannot construct, minted only through a slot's `i18n`, the
/// policy's `disclosure-fields`, and `enclavid:host-icons/icons`. The handle IS
/// the proof the key was declared, so membership needs no crypto token. A
/// plugin's helper that names a field takes the `disclosure-field-ref` the
/// policy minted. They live HERE (a shared interface) rather than inside each
/// interface that mints them, so every slot's `i18n` mints the SAME resource
/// type that the records a prompt is made of carry, and every version of
/// `enclavid:host-icons` mints the one `icon-ref` that `capture-step` carries.
interface refs {
    /// One of a component's texts, in every language its catalog has it in —
    /// surfaces as UI text once the host picks the applicant's language.
    resource localized-ref;
    /// An icon from `enclavid:host-icons/icons`, which the applicant
    /// frontend draws by its name.
    resource icon-ref;
    /// One of the policy's disclosure fields — surfaces as the machine
    /// `display-field.key` the consumer receives.
    resource disclosure-field-ref;
}
